  "text": "MOUSE OF REPRESE\nTHE PARLIAMENT OF THE COMMONWEALTH.\nFEDERAL MEMBERS' ROOMS,\nCOMMONWEALTH BANK BUILDING.\nPERTH, W.A.\n15th June, 1955.\nDear Mr. McFadyen,\nHeartiest congratulations on receiving the\nC.B.E. from Her Majesty The Queen.\nPersonally I can say that this honour has\nbeen well and truly earned and I am delighted to learn of your\nefforts being recognised.\nWith kindest regards.\nYours sincerely,\nden o Namiltoo\n(Len W. Hamilton, M.P.)\nParliamentary Under Secretary•\nMr. C.H. McFadyen, C.B.E.,\nDepartment of Shipping and Transport,\nMELBOURNE.\nVIC.\n\"Bona Vota\"\n59 mangland\n/1. 6. 53\nmany athers\nin expressing\ncongratulations\nthe necent honor bestowed\nwere dese\nTam sure i\n• deserved.\nRegard.\nyours\nser clady\nWare Sandbach",
